\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-13)^{8}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2(3x-13)^{8}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =16(3x-13)^{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-13)+0 \\\\  & =16(3x-13)^{7}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48(3x-13)^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186485729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45e0f19a-f9d5-5228-9b94-58ecab8e87eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485720} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2f5002-2107-58c8-b0a8-882b075d5cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485722} {:answer/id #uuid "a493d69f-2007-5ffc-875a-4c2592acbcbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485733} {:answer/id #uuid "be12a189-8ba2-5094-a4bd-2c96645a1c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485737} {:answer/id #uuid "e88c3d26-48cf-5e5e-aeb6-17a6ad386592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a493d69f-2007-5ffc-875a-4c2592acbcbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}(12-5x)^{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485733} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcc87777-afa0-5b4d-9e7c-63b17177db48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454